<section class="bg-paper">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 py-16">

    <div class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-ink p-6 flex gap-4" style="background:#C0392B14">
      <span class="text-2xl">⚠️</span>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">Elysium+ stands behind the European Parliament's recognition of the Russian Federation as a state sponsor of terrorism. This is our position as an organisation founded and still headquartered in Chernihiv — a region Russian forces occupied, besieged and bombed in 2022.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow mt-14" style="color:var(--coral-ink)">The European Parliament's position</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">A formal recognition, not a footnote</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">On 23 November 2022, the European Parliament adopted a resolution recognising the Russian Federation as a state sponsor of terrorism and a state that uses terrorist methods, by 494 votes to 58 with 44 abstentions. The resolution holds Russia responsible for deliberate attacks on Ukraine's civilian population and infrastructure, and states that its breaches of human rights and humanitarian law amount to acts of terror against the Ukrainian people and war crimes.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted text-sm">In the interest of accuracy: this is a political resolution of the European Parliament, not a binding legal designation — the EU currently has no formal legal mechanism for designating state sponsors of terrorism, and the resolution itself calls on the EU and its member states to create one. We state this plainly rather than overstate it, because getting the facts right matters to us as much as taking a position does.</p>
    <a href="https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/press-room/20221118IPR55707/european-parliament-declares-russia-to-be-a-state-sponsor-of-terrorism" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ink mt-6">Read the European Parliament's announcement {% icon "arrow-ur", "w-4 h-4" %}</a>

    <p class="eyebrow mt-16" style="color:var(--coral-ink)">Our home region</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">What happened in Chernihiv Oblast</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">Chernihiv city and the wider oblast were among the first places Russian forces attacked in February 2022, and among the most besieged in the war's opening weeks.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
      <div class="card p-6">
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">The siege of Chernihiv city</p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">From late February 2022, Russian forces surrounded Chernihiv and cut off most routes in and out. A bombing on 3 March killed 47 people — Amnesty International and Human Rights Watch both described the strike as a likely war crime. On 16 March, a Russian attack on civilians queuing for bread killed at least 18 people and injured 26 more. On 23 March, the last road bridge out of the city was destroyed, cutting off evacuation of the wounded and delivery of humanitarian aid.</p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/31/ukraine-civilians-besieged-chernihiv-need-access-essentials" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">Human Rights Watch, 31 Mar 2022</a>
          <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3_March_2022_Chernihiv_bombing" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">3 March 2022 bombing</a>
          <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/16_March_2022_Chernihiv_breadline_attack" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">16 March 2022 breadline attack</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6">
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">Yahidne: 28 days in a school basement</p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">On 3 March 2022, Russian soldiers occupying the village of Yahidne, Chernihiv Oblast, forced 368 residents — including 80 children, the youngest six weeks old — into the local school's basement, giving each person roughly 50cm of space. They were held there for 28 days, without adequate food, medical care, or ventilation. Ten people died in the basement; Ukrainian prosecutors have since charged Russian soldiers over those deaths.</p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://kyivindependent.com/audioguide-through-russian-occupation-of-yahidne-village-where-over-300-civilians-were-confined-in-school-basement/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">The Kyiv Independent</a>
          <a href="https://time.com/6255183/ukraine-basement-yahidne-held-captive/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">TIME</a>
          <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yahidne,_Chernihiv_Oblast" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">Background &amp; timeline</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6">
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">Documented across the oblast</p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">The UN Human Rights Monitoring Mission in Ukraine (OHCHR) has verified unlawful killings, including summary executions, of civilians in more than 30 settlements across Chernihiv Oblast while under Russian military control between late February and early April 2022 — part of a wider pattern OHCHR documented across more than 100 towns and villages in the Kyiv, Chernihiv and Sumy regions.</p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.ohchr.org/en/documents/country-reports/killings-civilians-summary-executions-and-attacks-individual-civilians" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">OHCHR report</a>
          <a href="https://ukraine.un.org/en/210727-killings-civilians-summary-executions-and-attacks-individual-civilians-kyiv-chernihiv-and" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">UN Ukraine summary</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow mt-16" style="color:var(--coral-ink)">The wider cost</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">Beyond one region</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">The Kyiv School of Economics Institute, working with Ukraine's Ministry for Development of Communities and Territories, estimates direct war damage to Ukraine's infrastructure at roughly $170 billion as of November 2024 — housing, transport and energy hit hardest, with 236,000 residential buildings damaged or destroyed nationwide. Chernihiv is named among the regions with the most severe damage.</p>
    <a href="https://kse.ua/about-the-school/news/damages-to-ukraine-s-infrastructure-due-to-the-war-have-risen-to-170-billion-kse-institute-estimate-as-of-november-2024/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ink mt-6">KSE Institute damage assessment {% icon "arrow-ur", "w-4 h-4" %}</a>

